<% content_for(:title) { "Recombinants · drosophila.me" } %>
<%= render "header", cross: @cross %>
<%= render "parents", cross: @cross %>
<%= render "tabs", cross: @cross, current: :recombinants %>
<p class="hint">
  Dashed cards carry a chromosome the mother could pass on after crossing over. Males don't recombine, so the father's chromosomes stay whole.
  These are possibilities, not predictions: without map positions the site can't give frequencies, and it can't tell when two alleles belong to the same gene.
  Name any balancer the site doesn't recognise in the cross's balancer list.
</p>
<%= render "chromosome_form", cross: @cross, recombinants: @recombinants %>
